{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored","id":827440,"title":"Repercussions of Chiminage not honored","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-10T05:35:20-08:00","id":827440,"title":"Repercussions of Chiminage not honored","content":"In a TT game I have a group of Garou that a few months ago turned to summoned Tribal Totems for aid in act of desperation (but for the betterment of Gaia), they each promised a lot in return should they have lived through the events. They did and now I have a couple of players that haven't kept up their side of the deal with the Spirits. Normally, they'd have to have something to give as chiminage first or there'd be a quest to gain this kind of favour in my games, but as above, was in a moment of desperation and they promised (tied themselves) to great acts in appreciation.<br /> <br /> I've pretty much got in mind what I need for a couple of them in the penance they must pay to their tribal totems as a warning to them and others never to short change a powerful spirit (Stag - a savagely brutal beating from a herd of spirits aligned with stag, maybe even a hunt. A month of no memory and no Knowledge's of anything for the Uktena after being dragged into darkness and then spat back out by his Totem). As well the Rite of Contrition. But I want there to be an actual cost or lesson, other than it appearing as if its just a rite and a roll to see how well it goes.<br /> <br /> But there is one Totem i'm having a bit of difficulty with, so please do feel free to give ideas (or even other ideas for the cost of not paying chiminage to powerful spirits), Unicorn. I guess it's the whole Peace and Mercy aspects of the Totem, especially to one of its own children.<br /> <br /> I'm currently thinking of having it come forward and just explain it forgives the character, but that other may not and have other spirits shun the character for they can not abide how Unicorn has been treated. Mirroring a bit of the CoGs own problems with society, others not being as accepting. I thought this was quite good as the character is a Theurge also.<br /> <br /> Any ideas, thoughts? any things you have done or seen others do towards Garou that fail to uphold their deals with spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T06:26:49-08:00","id":827467,"title":"","content":"First, a question. What was the wording of the chiminage? I would assume that the entire Pack would be responsible for paying back the debt unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> Second, Black Unicorn exists. If you piss off Unicorn badly enough, his avatar of war will run you through. Bonus: since Unicorn is the one who teaches Mother's Touch, the Gift won't be able to heal it.<br /> <br /> Third, <i>all</i> Spirits will be giving these Garou the Stinkeye for failing to deliver in a timely manner. Only the Pack Totem is likely to give them the time of day until all the debt is paid, and even afterward, getting Spirits to talk to them would be like <i>pulling teeth</i>. Spirit Notoriety is a very real thing and it sounds like these Garou have earned it. NOTE: This may necessitate an OOC conversation so that the players are on the same page as you about the punishment. They might feel like you're punishing the players for being unable to solve a problem you the GM created, rather than the game world punishing the PCs for failing to live up to their promises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:06:49-08:00","id":827514,"title":"","content":"Tribal totems all have broods and everyone of them will be on the look out for this pack. If I were handling this situation I'd probably give a warning to the players either out of character or in the game using dreams. I'd also strip them of renown and I'd probably do that first. Further I'd with hold renown particularly honor and wisdom until the spirits are satisfied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:12:38-08:00","id":827518,"title":"","content":"Thanks Etherial<br /> <br /> 1: Nah, not the pack (though they could choose to help), this is about one character under unicorn.<br /> <br /> 2: There's a Black unicorn spirit in the area but its not really its thing to harm someone who's likely sorry and of unicorns Tribe too and not wyrm tainted or has innocents that need protecting from. So I think using it would just be heavy handed and conflict with what the players have seen of it. <br /> <br /> 3: some of the pack have done their chiminage to their tribal totems and continued to give more. I dont want something thats going to last a long time. But still has aspects of unicorns temperment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:18:55-08:00","id":827527,"title":"","content":"Thanks incbill<br /> <br /> It's not the whole pack, just a few and this in particular is for Unicorn not receiving promised chiminage. Yeah, renown loss will be a thing among the garou for this, but I'm mostly interested in what Unicorn would exact from its failing child.<br /> <br /> I just dont see unicorn being as heavy handed or its brood going out to the garou over considering it corresponds with the concepts of mercy and Empathy. You know. There should be a price, although it could be interesting to see other individuals be treated harshly for their acts and unicorn just accepts the apology.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:29:22-08:00","id":827537,"title":"","content":"I also did think about Unicorn revoking mothers touch, but then I thought 'why would it allow for someone else to be in pain or need healing and not help just because of anothers actions?' And that didnt quite sit right with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:14:39-08:00","id":827555,"title":"","content":"Since Unicorn is all about healing, the Theurge seems to have Mothers Touch (most have anyway), and you want to punish the character and not anyone undeserving around him, I'd propose the following: untill he has made ammends, mothers touch and any other healing gifts just don't affect him positively. He can still cast it on anyone in need, but he himself will remain unhealed.<br /> <br /> If the offence was really, really great, you could even extend this into &quot;unicorns curse&quot;, to strip him of all his supernatural healing including his regeneration, till he pays the spirit back. He would still heal naturaly of course, but at the same rate as kinfolk/mortals (use with caution and only if the offence was truely great).<br /> <br /> That way, you can substantially punish the Garou, without withholding any help he may give to the needy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:36:21-08:00","id":827574,"title":"","content":"Thanks Seki<br /> <br /> The character doesn't have any Gifts that'll work on just him. I typically wouldnt have any objection to a Totem spirit revoking other abilities (like regeneration as you suggested), but how I've been portraying the SpIrit (high on healing, harmony, peace with an appreciation for Mercy and Purity) I just dont see it doing that. Especially as they fight the Wyrm often and putting the young child of gaia in a pposition where it could easily die against gaias enemies could be seen as doing something that aidsthe wyrm. Which I think the spirit would be conconscientious of as it's its Ban.<br /> <br /> I like that kind of thing, and have used similar repercussions before for other tribes...its just unicorn...Unicorn.<br /> <br /> I kind of think maybe the option of petitioning for another chiminage to make amends. Something to do with Wisdom and showing the character now understands the affects and impact of a garou not holding up their duties.<br /> <br /> If I cant think of something appropriate from Unicorns graceful wisdom then I may just apply a +1 difficulty on all spirit related tasks until the time of the original chiminage deal is over (another 6 months in game) as the spirits balk at the idea of helping one who has dishonored their agreement with Unicorn, but still aid in light of unicorns mercy...just not as easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:53:48-08:00","id":827618,"title":"","content":"I'm still kind of a newbie to werewolf, so let me know if this doesn't fit with the established cosmology. What do you think of the spirits ( or maybe just certain spirits ) refusing to honor and power rites that the theurge performs until they set things right with Unicorn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8365-pensman","name":"Pensman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8365_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:01:22-08:00","id":827685,"title":"","content":"I would not just make this about letting down a single totem spirit or it's brood... spirits are the primary allies of the Garou, and to piss them off or treat them with disrespect is courting disaster. The LARP has some nice rules for Infamy, which is basically penalties that rack up when you fail to keep your side of the bargain, but losing renown or even dire curses are also on the table, since what you are describing sounds less like a mistake and more like a royal fuckup. <br /> <br /> The penalties should be pretty dire, in my opinion. These Garou owe the totems their lives and they don't have the basic courtesy to repay something as fundamental as a lifedebt? What a bunch of dishonorable fools. Whatever happens, they deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:11:48-08:00","id":827692,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7706_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7706\" data-vbnamecard=\"7706\">Somuchlove</a> Well if punishment does not work for this specific spirit, I would go the opposite route.<br /> Make him make ammands.<br /> Let Unicorn guide the weak and the needy to him, so that hardly a day gets by without someone down on his luck comming to him, in dire need of his help.<br /> Let him see Unicorns reflection in the mirror, or flashing by on a random reflective surface in the area.<br /> If you really want to be obvious with it, let its image be spiritually superimposed uppon him. Or be subtle and don't show him at all, and let the player connect the dots.<br /> <br /> Alternatively pick a difficult situation, a quest if you will, of someone in need (or something else of interest for unicorn), and let unicorn come forth at the next moot and declare, that he expects the character to deal with it, no reward promised, no reknown to be earned, just repayment to unicorn in the currency it likes best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T12:33:50-08:00","id":827703,"title":"","content":"Just my opinion, but while Unicorn is forgiving, not honoring chiminage to is extremely disrespectful on the part of the Child. Totems do not suffer disrespect lightly. Even the &quot;nicer&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the idea of impeding said Garou's personal healing. I might've even gone so far as to remove all natural healing and require that they be magically healed.<br /> The +dif to all spirit related tasks could also be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Worth noting: even if Unicorn (or any of the Totems) does forgive, other spirits will still remember what was done (or failed to be done) and may be hesitant to make any pacts with the pack.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:33:48-08:00","id":828012,"title":"","content":"Other spirits will know they renege and react accordingly should they encounter them. Besides any special reactions you may do as ST, add +1 (or more) difficulty to ALL die rolls involving spirits.<br /> <br /> That kind of punishment is sublte, but ongoing, and relieves you of much of the burden of deciding what to do in many specific circumstances. That +1 difficulty will add up to a lot over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T01:30:56-08:00","id":828067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pensman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=827618#post827618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still kind of a newbie to werewolf, so let me know if this doesn't fit with the established cosmology. What do you think of the spirits ( or maybe just certain spirits ) refusing to honor and power rites that the theurge performs until they set things right with Unicorn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Pensman, thank you and welcome to your new life of hopefully enjoying Werewolf the Apocalypse!<br /> <br /> I do think something that hinders until repaired is the way, and utilising the gatous reIationship with spirits and the connectiin to Rites could ceetainly be a thing. Thank you for adding to the thread.<br /> <br /> @The Laughing Stranger<br /> Thank you for your input. I agree, other spirits should react to witnesding that an aspect of Unicorn, a Tribal totem has not been honored. If that's happening to Unicorn, how can those around or below expect to be tended to approproately in future? <br /> <br /> It wasn't a life debt though. Still pretty disrectful though. In game the cogs are thre number two tribe on the Sept and Unicorn the third most powerful and influential totem spirit. For it not to be paid its due and gain its promised chiminage (and Power from it)is a set back all will feel in some way.<br /> <br /> The Renown aspect has already been dealt with from the Garou standpoint, yes a loss heavily felt as honor and wisdom can be the most difficult to gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T02:05:57-08:00","id":828084,"title":"","content":"@Seki<br /> <br /> Thank you for coming back and adding more. Certainly some interesting ideas here, that I may use for others in the future, I especially like the mirror reflection perceptions and the potentially over whelming wave of people in need. I'm cautious of making it look like that others arent doing what they should, or that it could be passed off to others to deal with &quot;hey fellow coggies come help these people in trouble&quot; in what I would prefer to be a deeply personal lesson. But I like it.<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to offer the player options.<br /> Accept the chiminage has failed at a cost and take whats coming from the spurits.<br /> <br /> Apologise and ask for another chance to enact and honor a new chiminage in its place. Feeling the spirits (all spirits) displeasure until it is repaid under the original deals time to complete.<br /> <br /> @Idpersona<br /> Hi, thanks for joining in and adding your part. It's definitely helping seeing a few agree with the ideas and sentiments at the start of this. Definitely not something to take likely, incredibly disrespectful and fully agree.<br /> <br /> Though it's not really about being 'nice'. It's finding that balance and difficulty in acknowledging the repercussions when your portraying something otherworldly that represents the purest deepest aspects of Harmony (its tribe represented here will be affected, as will the Sept), Peace (why have it result or lead to aggression when surely it can uphold something greater, better), Healing (the next acts should be to heal the wound, the rift created), Mercy (Suffering and pain only feed the wyrm, I forgive but not forget and hope you'll grow to show the same consideration for others) and Purity to that and you have the most profound and dedicated spirit that will uphold those earlier beliefs and traits to its absolute highest ideals in form and function. Well, as well as I the ST can understand and portray them myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think in considering this, is why I'm not keen to have unicorn do anything physically to impede the character, especially in ways that reflects its mantra and core beliefs Healing being a big one any other Totem, yeah! But this one. It seems the opposite of what it is about..to me and in the incarnation of it I'm representing.<br /> <br /> But thank you, it is appreciated especially as you too do highlight the impact that couId come from other spirits. It gives it all the more weight to my decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T02:09:58-08:00","id":828085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=828012#post828012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other spirits will know they renege and react accordingly should they encounter them. Besides any special reactions you may do as ST, add +1 (or more) difficulty to ALL die rolls involving spirits.<br /> <br /> That kind of punishment is sublte, but ongoing, and relieves you of much of the burden of deciding what to do in many specific circumstances. That +1 difficulty will add up to a lot over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Black Fox. I think we've definitely come to shared opinion on this with regards to the impact to be felt and difficulties to face the character going forwards.<br /> <br /> Anyone else with any other ideas or input please do feel free to give them. Or even responses from my responses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll provide an update soon on how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T00:58:37-08:00","id":828655,"title":"","content":"Game update:<br /> <br /> Session began with a ooc discussion, as the characters had already felt the physical sting of punishment from their sept mates and elders for a shameful and costly act (Punishmemt rites and ostracism) I felt it good practice to advise them the spiritual repercussions of debts now unpayable would now be realised. But I assured there would be opportunity for redemption down the line for them to choose to commit to and hopefully succeed at.<br /> <br /> Those that had completed their chiminage were told this wouldnt affect them directly. But could possibly affect dealings with the pack.<br /> <br /> The players of characters that hadnt or no longer could complete their chiminage were given the options to try and make it better through apology and more chiminage (but that failing a second time would be truly a terrible thing), or take the consequences and move on with what ever hangs over them following.<br /> <br /> The Fianna decided to take what ever is coming. Deciding whoever failed to appease Stag deserved their kicking and as a Galliard was more than willng to be the story of warning for others to learn by.<br /> <br /> Nice. He got hunted by Black Stag and its crew. It wasnt pretty.<br /> <br /> The child of Gaia decided to try to apologise and offer more chiminage. I decided unicorn wasnt an emotional manipularor due to its concepts of empathy and didnt lay it too thickly but displayed great consideration and understanding in its forgiveness.<br /> <br /> The apology went perfectly (rite of contrition), but then the spirit turned the tables on the character &quot;last time I asked a chiminage of you. To learn from this (wisdom) I ask you to consider what you feel is appropriate chiminage for me on behalf of yourself to heal the tear between us.&quot;<br /> <br /> The player kind of struggled with that. Offering to be nice to other spirits. &quot;I expect that of all my children.&quot; Then offered to heal all those who required it that he came across &quot;as my child, would you not do this anyway?&quot; To give it all of his gnosis &quot;such a thing would help me, but would leave you weak, to weak to aid your pack and heal those who needed it more than I in the quests ahead of you.&quot; The player and character both seemed to be drowning. Unicorn offered guidance and the character asked please &quot;the wound between us cuts deeper than it appears. It will and does affect all of our Tribe here. To heal the damage down and honor me as your tribal patron a plentiful chiminage would be to do something that would bring a closer connection to my other children here. If you wish for my advice, take the opportunity of your quests to the umbra to find our tribal home, know it and bring back guiding hearts. One for each of my children here, so they too may be closer to me and have a way to always find their way to our Homeland.&quot;<br /> <br /> The player accepted and thanked the great spirit.<br /> <br /> Now, the reaction from the players was huge. Some had really struggled, some had made a lot of deals with others and endangered themselves to fulfill their obligations. Heck the fianna got hunted gored and nearly neutered by black Stags unrelenting force of punishment.<br /> <br /> There was outcry, there was shame, not at me but at the coggie character from the rest of the group, including its player. Why? Because unicorn was so pure, so good, so forgiving and understandable that realising the cost and failure in honoring such a spirit stung and cut a hunded times deeper than getting a royal beat down. <br /> <br /> Perfect! Unexpected but perfect. I now have a character and the rest of the pack with a high focus on doing all they can to ensure this is done once an opportunity arises.<br /> <br /> Mechanically I went with all spirits disdain for the character due to what the character has done to sacred and beloved unicorn is evident. +1 difficulty to all spirit related rolls. Thats social interaction, Gifts, Rites, even his own Numen spirit and Pack Totem until the new Chiminage is completed (6 months in game). Considering they are off to the Aetherial realms thats gonna sting. Lets hope he doesnt botch anything with a planerary incarna. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you to all who offered their input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T00:47:17-08:00","id":829164,"title":"","content":"Situations like these can be a tough balance to strike- you don't want to come off as a vindictive storyteller, punishing the players for basically doing WtA wrong, but at the same time, Garou thumbing their noses at tribal totems would be unconscionable. When the PCs undergo punishment, it is an opportunity to grow the characters while deepening the player's understanding of the setting, and it sounds like you accomplished that here.<br /> <br /> Good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T04:20:44-08:00","id":829199,"title":"","content":"That's exactly it The Laughing Stranger and thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T22:50:27-08:00","id":829589,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind, there was a second page all along!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T02:36:24-08:00","id":829629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=829589#post829589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Nevermind, there was a second page all along!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's ok Vysha, I didnt see it pre-edit but if you had something to add please feel that you can do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:38:26-07:00","id":875403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored#post827440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a TT game I have a group of Garou that a few months ago turned to summoned Tribal Totems for aid in act of desperation (but for the betterment of Gaia), they each promised a lot in return should they have lived through the events. They did and now I have a couple of players that haven't kept up their side of the deal with the Spirits. Normally, they'd have to have something to give as chiminage first or there'd be a quest to gain this kind of favour in my games, but as above, was in a moment of desperation and they promised (tied themselves) to great acts in appreciation.<br /> ..snip..<br /> Any ideas, thoughts? any things you have done or seen others do towards Garou that fail to uphold their deals with spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK first off (all quickly off the head before i read any other responses), all and any attempts to summon other spirits to aid them get a +2 difficulty penalty assigned to the gift/rites. <br /> You can also have Unicorn inform their sept master, and he can refuse to allow any rites to be performed till chimminage has been paid. <br /> And lastly, since unicorn is about healing/mercy, start having people show up to pester the party (Or pc) for healing consistently for say a few weeks in game..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=827467#post827467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, <i>all</i> Spirits will be giving these Garou the Stinkeye for failing to deliver in a timely manner. Only the Pack Totem is likely to give them the time of day until all the debt is paid, and even afterward, getting Spirits to talk to them would be like <i>pulling teeth</i>. Spirit Notoriety is a very real thing and it sounds like these Garou have earned it. NOTE: This may necessitate an OOC conversation so that the players are on the same page as you about the punishment. They might feel like you're punishing the players for being unable to solve a problem you the GM created, rather than the game world punishing the PCs for failing to live up to their promises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my above idea of making it harder to summon spirits in the first place..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=827555#post827555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Unicorn is all about healing, the Theurge seems to have Mothers Touch (most have anyway), and you want to punish the character and not anyone undeserving around him, I'd propose the following: untill he has made ammends, mothers touch and any other healing gifts just don't affect him positively. He can still cast it on anyone in need, but he himself will remain unhealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that suggestion. Heck if the Theurge has say a fetish pouch or leech tongue to use on himself perhaps that could malfunction for him as the spirit inside it rebels..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=828655#post828655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game update:<br /> <br /> ..snip..<br /> <br /> Now, the reaction from the players was huge. Some had really struggled, some had made a lot of deals with others and endangered themselves to fulfill their obligations. Heck the fianna got hunted gored and nearly neutered by black Stags unrelenting force of punishment.<br /> <br /> There was outcry, there was shame, not at me but at the coggie character from the rest of the group, including its player. Why? Because unicorn was so pure, so good, so forgiving and understandable that realising the cost and failure in honoring such a spirit stung and cut a hunded times deeper than getting a royal beat down.<br /> <br /> Perfect! Unexpected but perfect. I now have a character and the rest of the pack with a high focus on doing all they can to ensure this is done once an opportunity arises.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a very nicely done game and good outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:57:15-07:00","id":888984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=875403#post875403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK first off (all quickly off the head before i read any other responses), all and any attempts to summon other spirits to aid them get a +2 difficulty penalty assigned to the gift/rites. <br /> You can also have Unicorn inform their sept master, and he can refuse to allow any rites to be performed till chimminage has been paid. <br /> And lastly, since unicorn is about healing/mercy, start having people show up to pester the party (Or pc) for healing consistently for say a few weeks in game..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hence my above idea of making it harder to summon spirits in the first place..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like that suggestion. Heck if the Theurge has say a fetish pouch or leech tongue to use on himself perhaps that could malfunction for him as the spirit inside it rebels..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That was a very nicely done game and good outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Garhkal<br /> <br /> I really appreciate the ideas and insight, and thanks for praise on the outcome. I am blessed to have such a dedicated group of players who roll with the punches and continue to strive on even when things dont go as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:01:12-07:00","id":888985,"title":"","content":"As an update, the players characters have not only completed apologies and chiminage where needed. But also just completed a quest across the Atherial realm and completed chiminage to four Planetary incarna and survived Pangea.<br /> <br /> Now they return home, with enough renown to gain Fostern and hopefully new Deednames and shed the names of shame the septs Ragabash gave them after their punishment rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:46:40-07:00","id":889236,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the update! Love reading these stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:33:04-07:00","id":889324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=888984#post888984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you Garhkal<br /> <br /> I really appreciate the ideas and insight, and thanks for praise on the outcome. I am blessed to have such a dedicated group of players who roll with the punches and continue to strive on even when things dont go as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help out!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T06:07:52-07:00","id":889824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=889236#post889236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the update! Love reading these stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> cool. Well then allow me to share more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The story begins three months after the Pack received their punishments. Stripped of rank and privileges the characters as Cliath have spent the time as the Omegas to the Sept. They have been doing all the duties and chores no one else wants. No others, not Garou or Kin have socialised with them and they have not been allowed to speak at Moots nor even leave the Bawn in all that time (we didnt RP through all of this, as that would not have been fun at all for anyone. We just Fast Forwarded).<br /> <br /> Words and stories from around the Nation have been reaching the Sept and seemingly shared in similar tragedies of late. Tales of natural disasters across the Globe, An army of BSDs under the banner of the Metis born child of destiny levelling Caerns, and most disturbing, no new children to the Nation. All kin and Garou pregnant have sadly lost their precious packages before being able to give birth. <br /> <br /> Whispers and accusations point to the Apocalypse, and more than a few fingers point at our pack as being responsible for the turn of events. The only thing keeping them alive, is proof that their actions indeed did cause this turn of events.<br /> <br /> Theurges and those with spirit sensitive abilities through the Kinfolk have been plagued with terrible nightmares of things of the past, the preseht and the futures. The two common themes, a child that should not be, and a Red Star in the sky.<br /> <br /> The Nation has responded. More information must be gained. Insights and answers must be known and the Septs that can are sending packs to the Aetherial realm to gain that which is needed for the coming nights.<br /> <br /> Each Sept holds their challenges. Trials of Glory, Honor and Wisdom to test their packs and see which shall carry the Septs names to the Stars and Planetary Incarna themselves. <br /> <br /> Out of 5 npc packs and our stories player Pack they came third. Gaining the right to once again leave the Sept, Quest on behalf of the Nation and maybe, just maybe, redeem themselves in the process. (This we did RP through <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Each Pack chose four incarna with which to seek out as best for their abilities and alignments of Tribe and Auspice.<br /> <br /> The Pack chose, Helios, Meros, Vulcan, Ruatma and began their journey under the patronage of their pack Totem Owl.<br /> <br /> More to come. ..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:34:21-07:00","id":890085,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the players handled it all very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:40:08-07:00","id":890147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/827440-repercussions-of-chiminage-not-honored?p=890085#post890085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the players handled it all very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did! And considering that for each of them it's either their first time playing or first time playing it to serious themes (and by that I mean not just hack and slash, give me powoars!!) it's very impressive and refreshing to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T14:17:24-07:00","id":890169,"title":"","content":"First stop. Meros.<br /> The Pack chose to begin at the furthest reaches of the Realm and the final Planetary incarna and make their way back through the list and back home. Taking great efforts in using rites, rituals, gifts and benefits of Owl to begin their journey unseen and undetected. The way there is full of sights to behold, incredible sights that leave the Pack lost for words and starting to realise just how magnanimous the powers of the Heavens are, and how dangerous.<br /> <br /> Through a group combination of astrolohical rites, enigmas and cosmology, the Coggie Theurge and Strider Ahroun find the right paths and lead the pack into Meros' busy domain of travellers and celestial storms. The place is very busy, but a special road is laid out for them that leads to an oasis. <br /> <br /> With an offering, Meros, a 30ft gold and jewel adorned Anubis formed road traveller arives. They ask for his aid, his wisdom and his guidance. <br /> <br /> He asks of them their story and purpose.<br /> They offer chiminage of his chosing.<br /> He tells them he will help them now, but not give the answers they search for until his chiminage is completed.<br /> They agree.<br /> He gives them a chance to practice how to speak and address Planetary incarnas. He tells them the best way to begin appropriately on a quest within the Realm is to visit either Hekios of Luna first. He shows them which road to take.<br /> <br /> He tells his chiminage is the story of the Journey at their end, he is pleased to be there at the beginning but seeing them and hearing how their journey went will be their Chiminage to him.<br /> <br /> They ask if they may have one question of importance each now. He smiles and agrees but only if they tell him how they see themselves now, and what they hope to gain from their journey.<br /> <br /> His answers about the child, the coming days of the Apocalypse, the nature of prophesy and what he believes it to mean...shake them deeply.<br /> <br /> Next<br /> <br /> Helios","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}